  "problem": "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -10 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} .",
  "worked_solution": "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|6\\cdot 3-(-10)\\cdot (-5)| \\\\  & =|18-50| \\\\  & =|-32| \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
